## Final acceptance

☐ `ds.mount()` attaches non-owningly to the exact current native DF viewscreen.
☐ Native and overlay controls are accessible through the common fluent subject
  API.
☐ Native subjects safely expose typed userdata, paths, bounds, state, text,
  pointer placement, input, and redraw.
☐ Existing component mounts retain their prior behavior.
☐ Normal DFHack focus, screen-stack, overlay input, and render behavior are
  preserved.
☐ Every retained subject and attached screen has explicit staleness behavior.
☐ Cleanup restores all DwarfSpec instrumentation and pointer/button state.
☐ DwarfSpec never owns or dismisses the native screen or registered overlays.
☐ Runtime declarations and user documentation match the implemented behavior.
☐ All checklist items and evidence-ledger entries are complete.
